    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0019_b3a51aaaefc4.png\" style=\"width:1.72014in;height:1.66667in\" /><br />Let, top of the tower is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math>,&nbsp;foot of the tower is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F,</mi></math>&nbsp;height of the tower is <math><mi>h</mi></math> &amp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∠</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>θ</mi></math><br />Because <math><mi>T</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>F</mi></math> is a right-angled <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi></math></p><p>so,&nbsp;<math><mi>P</mi><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cot</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></math>,</p><p>similarly,&nbsp;<math><mi>Q</mi><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>S</mi><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cot</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo></math> points&nbsp;<math><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>S</mi></math> lie on the same circle<br /><math><mo>⇒</mo></math> points&nbsp;<math><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>S</mi></math> are vertices of a cyclic quadrilateral but may or may not be consecutive vertices in the same order<br />Hence, options&nbsp;<math><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>B</mi></math> &amp; <math><mi>D</mi></math> may or may not be correct.<br />But, option <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is always correct</p>"
  }
}